; One executable per module under test; they all share the Support fixtures
; and testables. Nothing here opens a window. Framebuffer.offscreen builds a
; buffer with no streaming texture behind it, and Renderer.draw_frame fills one
; with no SDL call in it, so test_renderer draws whole frames and reads the
; pixels back — as do test_paint and test_font. Only Renderer.render itself,
; which is the upload and the present, is left untested, and there is nothing in
; it but those two calls. Input reads SDL for the keyboard and the mouse, but
; its edges and hold timer are a pure function of two frames and a duration, and
; test_input drives that directly; Binding turns such a frame into a movement
; and touches nothing at all, so test_binding drives that.
;
; The demo's suites live here too, beside the engine's own, because they share
; these fixtures and there is no reason to run them separately. A game built on
; this engine tests itself in its own repo.

; The suites that load pictures read them from fixtures/ by plain relative
; path, because dune runs a test with its working directory here — so the
; loaders are tested without going through Asset, and Asset is tested without
; going near SDL. The demos' own art comes in through Asset, which is why the
; whole of assets/ is a dependency too: test_demos builds every demo's world,
; and one of them reads files.

(tests
 (deps
  (glob_files fixtures/*)
  (source_tree ../assets))
 (names
  test_vec
  test_result_ext
  test_asset
  test_surface
  test_paint
  test_renderer
  test_font
  test_plane
  test_sky
  test_image
  test_transform
  test_room
